    "findings": [
      "Reviewed 4 of 84 captures directly (home dark/light desktop, home high-contrast mobile, status dark desktop). No UI changed this session, so this recapture exists to rebind the receipt to the resealed candidate manifest (D-S338.5), not to clear a CANON-053 obligation. Rendering, hierarchy and contrast are sound in every capture inspected; the mobile drawer trigger renders correctly at 390px with no sticky or broken menu. One PRE-EXISTING defect observed and NOT introduced here: the home portfolio cards render a doubled status label - a SPARKED pill with a second orange SPARKED beneath it, clipped to a bare S on the smaller tiles. It is client-rendered (no SPARKED badge exists in the static markup) and appears identically in dark and light, so it is not an animation frame. Recorded on the board rather than fixed, because changing UI would invalidate every hash-bound receipt immediately before the authorized production deploy."
    ],
